-- title:
--   Base change of mod-p modular functions along a field map
-- statement:
--   Let $K_0$ and $K$ be fields, $\iota : K_0 \to K$ a ring homomorphism, $m$ a natural number, and $G$ a Laurent series over $K_0$. Write $\bar j_F := \mathrm{jqModC}\,F$ for the Laurent series over a field $F$ obtained as $q^{-1}$ times the image under $\mathbb{Z} \to F$ of the fixed integral power series `jNum`. Assume `IsModPFormFn K₀ m G`, that is: $G^6\,\bar j_{K_0}^{4m}\,(\bar j_{K_0} - 1728)^{3m}$ is integral over the $K_0$-subalgebra of $K_0((q))$ generated by $\bar j_{K_0}$, and $G^2\,\bar j_{K_0}^{m}\,(\bar j_{K_0} - 1728)^{m}$ is integral over the $K_0$-subalgebra generated by $\bar j_{K_0}^{-1}$ (the constants $1728$ being the images of $1728 \in K_0$ under the structure map). The conclusion is that `IsModPFormFn K m` holds for $\mathrm{coeffMap}\,\iota\,G$, the Laurent series over $K$ obtained by applying $\iota$ to each coefficient of $G$: the two corresponding products formed from $\mathrm{coeffMap}\,\iota\,G$ and $\bar j_K$ are integral over $K[\bar j_K]$ and over $K[\bar j_K^{-1}]$ respectively. No hypothesis is imposed on $K_0$, $K$ or $\iota$ beyond their being fields and a ring homomorphism.
--
--   This is the base-change statement for the integrality formulation of "holomorphic mod-$p$ modular function of weight $2m$": the property is preserved by pushing $q$-expansion coefficients forward along any homomorphism of fields. It is used to transport the comparison between classical $q$-expansions and mod-$p$ modular functions from a prime field to an arbitrary field of the same characteristic, and is invoked in the results relating elements of the mod-$p$ modular forms modules to weight-graded $q$-expansions.
